 "capsule": "\"Holy Roman Empire Minor States\" denotes the empire's dense mosaic of small imperial estates — free imperial cities, prince-bishoprics, imperial abbeys, and petty counties — whose practical autonomy hardened after the Great Interregnum of 1250–1273 left the imperial crown weak relative to its territorial princes. Formally organized as Reichsstände with seats and votes in the Imperial Diet, these minor territories multiplied through partible inheritance and religious partition, and hundreds of them survived in diminished form until Napoleon's Reichsdeputationshauptschluss of 1803 and the empire's dissolution in 1806.",
